msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Contributing to this project\n"
"\n"
"First of all, thank you for taking the time to contribute to this project. Your support is the driving force behind our continuous improvement.\n"
"\n"
"The following guidelines are intended to help you participate in this project smoothly and efficiently. Please read them carefully before contributing.\n"
"\n"
"## Table of Contents\n"
"\n"
"- [Contribution Methods](#contribution-methods)\n"
"- [Development Process](#development-process)\n"
"- [Code Style](#code-style)\n"
"- [Commit Message Guidelines](#commit-message-guidelines)\n"
"- [Issue Reporting Guidelines](#issue-reporting-guidelines)\n"
"- [Pull Request Guidelines](#pull-request-guidelines)\n"
"- [Code Review Process](#code-review-process)\n"
"- [Community and Communication](#community-and-communication)\n"
"\n"
"## Contribution Methods\n"
"\n"
"You can contribute to this project in the following ways:\n"
"\n"
"- Report bugs or provide suggestions by submitting Issues\n"
"- Submit code improvements via Pull Requests\n"
"- Improve project documentation\n"
"- Help answer questions from other users\n"
"- Share and promote this project\n"
"\n"
"## Development Process\n"
"\n"
"1. Fork the repository to your own account\n"
"2. Clone the forked repository to your local machine\n"
"3. Create a new branch for development\n"
"4. Make code changes and ensure the code passes tests\n"
"5. Submit a Pull Request to the main repository\n"
"\n"
"## Code Style\n"
"\n"
"- Follow the existing code style and conventions of the project\n"
"- Ensure the code is readable and maintainable\n"
"- Add necessary comments, but avoid excessive comments\n"
"- Keep the code concise and avoid unnecessary complexity\n"
"\n"
"## Commit Message Guidelines\n"
"\n"
"- Use clear and descriptive commit messages\n"
"- Follow the format: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`\n"
"- Common types include: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, etc.\n"
"\n"
"## Issue Reporting Guidelines\n"
"\n"
"When reporting an Issue, please provide the following information:\n"
"\n"
"- A clear description of the problem\n"
"- Steps to reproduce the issue\n"
"- Expected behavior and actual behavior\n"
"- Environment information (operating system, version, etc.)\n"
"- Relevant code snippets or error messages\n"
"\n"
"## Pull Request Guidelines\n"
"\n"
"1. Ensure the PR description clearly states the purpose and content of the changes\n"
"2. Keep the PR scope focused and avoid mixing multiple unrelated changes\n"
"3. Ensure all tests pass and add new tests for new features\n"
"4. Update relevant documentation\n"
"5. Reference related Issue numbers\n"
"\n"
"## Code Review Process\n"
"\n"
"- All code changes require review and approval from maintainers\n"
"- Reviewers will provide feedback and suggestions within a reasonable time\n"
"- Please respond promptly to review comments and make necessary modifications\n"
"- Once the review is approved, the maintainer will merge the changes\n"
"\n"
"## Community and Communication\n"
"\n"
"- Follow the community code of conduct and maintain a friendly and professional communication atmosphere\n"
"- Respect the opinions and contributions of other community members\n"
"- Use clear and concise language when communicating\n"
"- If you encounter problems, feel free to ask for help in the community\n"
"\n"
"Thank you again for your contribution! Together, let's make this project better.\n"

